Subject: [INGENIA build tests] portable musl UTC input and offline HTTP fixture

Only test inputs change; all original success/file/time assertions remain.
Apply after Alpine 0022, retaining numeric UTC and all DST/offset checks.
Four wget tests use the bounded Python loopback HTTP fixture.

--- a/testsuite/date/date-timezone
+++ b/testsuite/date/date-timezone
@@ -3,2 +3,2 @@
-# 'Z' is UTC
-dt=$(TZ=UTC busybox date -d '1999-1-2 3:4:5Z')
+# Numeric UTC is portable to musl strptime(%z).
+dt=$(TZ=UTC busybox date -d '1999-1-2 3:4:5 +0000')
--- a/testsuite/wget/wget--O-overrides--P
+++ b/testsuite/wget/wget--O-overrides--P
@@ -4 +4 @@
-busybox wget -q -O index.html -P foo http://www.google.com/
+busybox wget -q -O index.html -P foo http://127.0.0.1:18080/
--- a/testsuite/wget/wget-handles-empty-path
+++ b/testsuite/wget/wget-handles-empty-path
@@ -3 +3 @@
-busybox wget http://www.google.com
+busybox wget http://127.0.0.1:18080
--- a/testsuite/wget/wget-retrieves-google-index
+++ b/testsuite/wget/wget-retrieves-google-index
@@ -3 +3 @@
-busybox wget -q -O foo http://www.google.com/
+busybox wget -q -O foo http://127.0.0.1:18080/
--- a/testsuite/wget/wget-supports--P
+++ b/testsuite/wget/wget-supports--P
@@ -4 +4 @@
-busybox wget -q -P foo http://www.google.com/
+busybox wget -q -P foo http://127.0.0.1:18080/
